 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Not at all. Many people start then, and few have any competitive advantage. You just need consistency and finding way that works for you. Then start with simple phrases that show off your unique way of saying things instead. People enjoy the surprise more than well grained but boring one. Nice. Portuguese is a beautiful language. Great. Start with simple phrases you hear on every trip, like How much is this one worth, and The waiter speaks good English. Start at the basics. Who am I? Where am I from? What do you do for fun? Ask someone to lunch in English, so you get practice without feeling like a beginner.",
